  "body": "As discussed in https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/546 and https://github.com/whatwg/url/pull/284, we'd like to add the [dangling markup injection mitigation](https://chromestatus.com/feature/5735596811091968) to the HTML spec (which was implemented in Chromium for ~ 6 years).\n\nThis PR makes the following changes:\n\n1. Add and implement the dangling markup injection mitigation in the `check dangling markup` algorithm.\n2. Add `HTML-parse a URL` algorithm which calls the `check dangling markup` algorithm before parsing.\n3. Add `HTML-encoding-parsing-and-serialize a URL` algorithm which has same logic as [HTML-encoding-parsing-and-serializing a URL](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#encoding-parsing-and-serializing-a-url) except it uses `HTML-parse a URL` algorithm above.\n4. Re-route all dangling markup injection sinks to use `check dangling markup`-backed algorithms.\n\nI have not modified the [module specifier resolution](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#module-specifier-resolution), since it has a strict grammer and it's most likely to not result in a successful dangling markup injection.\n\nI hope this change covers all of the scope we are interested in 😊 And going forward, any potential dangling markup injection sinks should call the `check dangling markup`-backed algorithms.\n\nFixes: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10021\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium\n   * Gecko https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10022#issuecomment-2058795635\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/44466\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/43808\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=680970\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1899514\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=172748\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: Not necessary (`<` and whitespace are [not valid](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#url-code-points) in URLs).\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7)\">/common-dom-interfaces.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/055a678...fdbc1e7/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/form-control-infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7)\">/form-control-infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/055a678...fdbc1e7/form-control-infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/iframe-embed-object.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7)\">/iframe-embed-object.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/055a678...fdbc1e7/iframe-embed-object.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/10022/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 30, 2024, 11:26 AM UTC (fdbc1e7